You fill in all your details and preferences, like if you are a smoker or if you have any pets.

22
00:01:01,400 --> 00:01:04,860
Then you find people that have similar characteristics and you can email them or chat.

23
00:01:05,840 --> 00:01:06,640
That's kind of weird.

24
00:01:07,600 --> 00:01:09,660
What if she's a psycho or something like that?

25
00:01:10,440 --> 00:01:12,600
It's the same as meeting people anywhere and dating them.

26
00:01:12,960 --> 00:01:16,220
I'm just tired of going to bars or being set up for dates by my friends.

27
00:01:16,700 --> 00:01:19,660
I think this is a really cool alternative, especially if you are a bit shy.

28
00:01:20,380 --> 00:01:21,820
I guess it does seem logical.

29
00:01:22,520 --> 00:01:23,480
I'll have to check it out.

30
00:01:27,080 --> 00:01:28,080
All right.

31
00:01:28,080 --> 00:01:29,080
We're back.

32
00:01:29,080 --> 00:01:35,240
Now, let's take a look at some of these key words that we've picked out for you on Language Takeaway.

33
00:01:35,240 --> 00:01:35,870
Language Takeaway.

34
00:01:38,120 --> 00:01:45,440
The first word is a word that you're going to hear English speakers say all the time, especially if they're Americans.

35
00:01:45,440 --> 00:01:46,430
Cool is our first word.

36
00:01:47,120 --> 00:01:51,570
This guy described this girl that he is seeing as really cool.

37
00:01:51,750 --> 00:01:52,510
She's really cool.

38
00:01:53,040 --> 00:01:56,220
What does that mean if I describe someone as a cool person?

39
00:01:56,620 --> 00:01:58,880
A cool person is someone who you like.

40
00:01:59,280 --> 00:01:59,800
It's a good thing.

41
00:02:00,100 --> 00:02:06,920
Someone who is cool, I think of as relaxed and interesting and someone who maybe has lots of ideas or things to say.

42
00:02:07,860 --> 00:02:11,540
If you say that a person is cool, you're saying that you like that person.

43
00:02:12,020 --> 00:02:15,400
What if you say something is cool, like Paris is really cool?

44
00:02:15,750 --> 00:02:16,570
Paris is cool.

45
00:02:16,850 --> 00:02:17,650
It's a cool city.

46
00:02:18,000 --> 00:02:19,920
That means it's an interesting city.

47
00:02:19,920 --> 00:02:20,850
It's something that you like.

48
00:02:21,920 --> 00:02:24,030
Maybe you're trying to recommend someone to go there.

49
00:02:24,720 --> 00:02:26,590
You can also say that movie was really cool.

50
00:02:26,970 --> 00:02:28,710
So again, it means you liked it.

51
00:02:29,520 --> 00:02:30,520
Yeah.

52
00:02:30,520 --> 00:02:31,520
Okay.

53
00:02:31,520 --> 00:02:38,440
So talking about dating, this friend was a bit surprised when he said that he met this girl online.

54
00:02:38,440 --> 00:02:39,440
That's right.

55
00:02:39,440 --> 00:02:41,640
So online, where is this place online?

56
00:02:41,860 --> 00:02:42,700
It's in cyberspace.

57
00:02:43,180 --> 00:02:43,420
All right.

58
00:02:43,960 --> 00:02:45,960
So online means on the internet.

59
00:02:45,960 --> 00:02:48,920
And we often use this when describing things.

60
00:02:48,920 --> 00:02:53,620
So EnglishPod is an online English learning site.

61
00:02:53,820 --> 00:02:54,260
That's right.

62
00:02:54,500 --> 00:02:58,780
So anything that is in the internet, in cyberspace, you say that is online.

63
00:02:59,320 --> 00:03:00,680
So our website is online.

64
00:03:01,240 --> 00:03:02,440
Or maybe you have pictures online.

65
00:03:02,900 --> 00:03:04,520
I have many photographs online.

66
00:03:04,520 --> 00:03:06,100
Or I like to meet people online.

67
00:03:06,640 --> 00:03:06,940
Okay.

68
00:03:07,600 --> 00:03:15,480
So continuing on, we talked about a website that obviously that's online where you find people and talking about preferences.

69
00:03:16,340 --> 00:03:20,020
You mentioned that you can state whether you are a smoker or if you have pets.

70
00:03:20,540 --> 00:03:22,340
So what is a person that's a smoker?

71
00:03:22,910 --> 00:03:27,190
Well, many of you have probably heard the term to smoke before.

72
00:03:27,440 --> 00:03:28,230
I smoke cigarettes.

73
00:03:28,520 --> 00:03:29,740
I smoke.

74
00:03:29,740 --> 00:03:32,470
But a smoker is a person who smokes cigarettes.

75
00:03:32,800 --> 00:03:37,980
And so I could say that I want a non-smoker if I'm looking for a boyfriend.

76
00:03:37,980 --> 00:03:40,520
Because I don't want someone who smokes.

77
00:03:40,520 --> 00:03:44,920
But maybe if you do smoke, you can say I'm looking for a smoker, someone who does smoke.

78
00:03:44,920 --> 00:03:45,920
Okay.

79
00:03:45,920 --> 00:03:48,070
So Jen was a little bit concerned saying, well, that's weird.

80
00:03:48,360 --> 00:03:51,800
What if this girl is a psycho or something like that?

81
00:03:52,030 --> 00:03:52,490
All right.

82
00:03:52,800 --> 00:03:53,210
A psycho.

83
00:03:53,800 --> 00:03:55,590
Now, maybe you've heard of the movie Psycho.

84
00:03:56,560 --> 00:04:02,470
But psycho is something that we use in English to say that someone is really crazy, almost scary crazy.

85
00:04:02,920 --> 00:04:04,730
It comes from the word psychopath, right?

86
00:04:05,050 --> 00:04:05,470
That's right.

87
00:04:06,320 --> 00:04:09,120
And a psychopath is someone who is crazy but also very dangerous.

88
00:04:09,120 --> 00:04:10,120
Right.

89
00:04:10,120 --> 00:04:14,950
So obviously when we use this word, we're describing someone as being a little bit strange or maybe even a little bit dangerous.

90
00:04:15,560 --> 00:04:15,710
That's right.

91
00:04:16,560 --> 00:04:20,530
So we don't want any psychos to come and talk to us online, right?

92
00:04:20,920 --> 00:04:21,150
That's right.

93
00:04:22,120 --> 00:04:26,770
So he went on to explain how dating is just the same online as it is offline.

94
00:04:27,800 --> 00:04:32,080
And that he thinks it's a really cool alternative, even if you're shy.

95
00:04:32,080 --> 00:04:35,470
So something is an alternative if you have different options.

96
00:04:36,720 --> 00:04:40,990
Maybe dating by going to a bar and meeting someone is what normal people do.

97
00:04:41,820 --> 00:04:44,690
But an alternative to that would be dating online.

98
00:04:45,320 --> 00:04:45,510
That's right.

99
00:04:46,320 --> 00:04:46,830
It's another option.

100
00:04:47,320 --> 00:04:50,750
So the word alternative is a second option, another option.

101
00:04:51,040 --> 00:04:52,040
Right.

102
00:04:52,040 --> 00:04:58,160
For example, if I want to go have Italian food tonight, but you don't want to, I'd say, Hey, Marco, well, can you give me an alternative idea?

103
00:04:58,160 --> 00:04:59,430
That is the other option.

104
00:05:00,460 --> 00:05:00,740
All right.

105
00:05:00,780 --> 00:05:00,960
Great.

106
